The Basics
Instead of playing, one player is chosen to run the game and will be referred to as the Host. In the game, everyone receives a role card, which they may not show to any other players and must place face-down in front of themself. The game has a cycle of two phases: night and day, starting with night.
At night, all players must close their eyes while the Host calls on certain players/roles to perform an action.
During the day, all players may open their eyes and discuss. At the end of the day, one player is chosen to be lynched. When the day ends is up to the Host. All players must vote at the same time by pointing at who they wish to lynch. Whoever receives the most votes is eliminated. Eliminated players do not participate in the game anymore and are allowed to keep their eyes open during nights. In case of a tie, nobody dies.
Each player's goal depends on their role card, though generally players must eliminate all players from a different team. Usually players will reveal their cards on death, though in some rule variants this does not occur.

